  "body": "With a provenance reaching back to the 1940s, this Kiwi archetype is ready to again welcome a family. Set back from the street and nestled in charming, manicured gardens, the generous  three-bedroom home integrates versatile spaces inside and out, irresistible for growing families and busy professionals alike. \r\n\r\nThe three level residence retains many features typical of the era. Crisp white walls, original native wood floors and elegant mood lighting set the scene adding a subtle Tuscan villa vibe. Open plan living is warm in winter with log burner fireplace and a wall mounted heat pump working to deliver year-round comfort. Bifolds stack back easing the flow to a deck with clear roof pergola and built in seating ready for alfresco entertaining while terrace gardens accentuate the picturesque outlook. A light and airy dining area accompanies an open plan kitchen with Dish Drawer, underbench oven and some scope to upgrade if desired. The bathroom on this floor has shower system in edgy black, while the main bathroom upstairs includes a bathtub. This serves three bedrooms each with built in wardrobes and has central heating and cooling on this level. On the ground floor, a substantial rumpus room with heat pump and its own entrance lends itself for a range of uses. The storage rooms and adaptable spaces offer more possibilities to rework. \r\n\r\nOff street parking abuts flat lawns on the beautifully landscaped and tree lined section. Quiet and tranquil yet close to Eastridge shopping centre, and the bustling beach precincts, this affordable entry-level bays' property is desirably zoned for nearby Orakei and Kohimarama Schools as well as Selwyn College. \r\n\r\nOur owners are now based overseas and committed to sale. Don't miss this opportunity for an affordable entry to The Bays!",
